# BeautyBook Project Conventions

## TypeScript

- Keep `strict: true`; no `any` unless unavoidable — prefer explicit types and Prisma-generated types from `@/app/generated/prisma`.
- Use `@/` path aliases for imports.
- Server actions that back `<form action={...}>` must return `void` or `Promise<void>`; use `ActionFormState` + `useActionState` (via `ActionForm`) when returning validation errors to the client. Shared types live in `lib/action-form-state.ts`.

## React / Next.js

- Functional components only — no class components.
- Default to **Server Components**; add `"use client"` only for hooks, browser APIs, or client interactivity.
- Mutations: **server actions** in colocated `actions.ts` files, not ad-hoc REST routes (except Better Auth `/api/auth/*` and future webhooks).
- Auth gates: `requireUser()` for signed-in pages, `requireOrgMember()` for tenant-specific actions, `requireActiveOrgContext()` for member dashboard, and `requireActiveOrgAdmin()` (or `requireAdmin()` alias) for `/dashboard/admin/*`. Organization admin access is strictly governed by `OrgRole` (`OWNER` or `ADMIN`); `User.role === ADMIN` does not grant access.
- After mutations: `revalidatePath()` for affected routes, then `redirect()` on success.

## Styling (Tailwind only)

- Use Tailwind utility classes — no CSS modules, styled-components, or inline `style={}`.
- Global tokens live in `app/globals.css` (`@import "tailwindcss"`); keep the app on the light theme (`color-scheme: light`).
- Reuse shared classes from `lib/ui.ts` (`controlClass`, `primaryButtonClass`, `errorAlertClass`, etc.) for forms and buttons.
- Text on inputs/selects: always set explicit light-theme colors (`text-zinc-900`, `bg-white`).

## Prisma / database

- **Single entry point:** import `prisma` from `@/lib/prisma` — never instantiate `PrismaClient` elsewhere.
- Business logic that queries the DB belongs in `lib/` (e.g. `lib/booking.ts`, `lib/schedule.ts`, `lib/catalog.ts`), not scattered in components.
- Use generated enums from `@/app/generated/prisma/enums` (`Role`, `OrgRole`, `AppointmentStatus`, `Weekday`).
- Pin Prisma 7.x; avoid Prisma 8 RC. No schema change without a migration.
- **`postinstall`** runs `prisma generate`; `/app/generated/prisma` is gitignored.
- **Supabase Postgres** (storage only — not Supabase Auth): default **`DATABASE_URL`** is the **session pooler** URI (`*.pooler.supabase.com:5432`, user `beautybook_prisma.[REF]`). Use `npx prisma migrate deploy` on hosted DB (not `migrate dev`). Raw SQL migrations (e.g. exclusion constraints) may need Supabase SQL editor + `migrate resolve` if pooler DDL fails.
- Schema integrity: `Location_one_default_per_org` enforces **at most one default location per organization** via a partial unique index (`WHERE isDefault = true`).
- `priceCents` is integer centavos (PHP display via `formatPrice` in `lib/format.ts`).
- Soft-deactivate with `active: false`; do not hard-delete rows referenced by appointments.

## Money & locale

- Display prices with `formatPrice()` — currency is **PHP** (`en-PH`).
- Parse admin price inputs with `parsePesoToCentavos()` from `lib/catalog.ts`.

## Testing & Safety

- Verify scripts: `npm run verify` (runs all 11 verification checks — strictly fail-closed; requires an approved local test database; no remote bypass).
- E2E: `npm run test:e2e` (Playwright suite of 34 tests — seeds local test DB via `global-setup.ts`).
- Demo accounts: `lib/demo-account.ts` (all passwords `Demo1234!`):
  - `demo@beautybook.local` (Owner/Admin)
  - `customer@beautybook.local` (Customer)
  - `owner@glow-nails.local` / `owner@luxe-hair.local` (Marketplace owners)

## Validation

- Use Zod schemas in `lib/validations/` for new server actions; `safeParse` + `actionError` on failure.
- Legacy `parse*` helpers in `lib/catalog.ts` remain for existing forms until migrated.
